<!--
  The source chooser, in Dutch.

  Its strings lived only in `values/` and `values-ar/`, so every other language
  rendered this screen in English while the rest of the application was translated.
  A screen half in the reader's language is worse than one consistently in another:
  it reads as a fault rather than as a limit.

  Kept short on purpose. The two cards under the rule are half the width of the two
  above them and hold one line of description each; a detail and a hint that together
  run past that line are cut on the device. The English and Arabic were measured at
  the television's own column before they were settled, and these follow them.
-->
